invariant: INV-16
file: src/p256_wide_inverse.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh p256_wide_inverse_steps
reason: the steps that count the zeros above the top bit of a | b test one
  bit more than each moves, so the count stops a bit short, the top bit of
  a | b ends at bit 126 of the pair and an approximation keeps 32 of the
  value's top bits where the bound spec/lean/Spec/P256WideInverse.lean
  proves reads 33. p256_wide_inverse_steps holds the approximations to a
  reference that reads the 33 bits from the bit length of a | b, over every
  a and b. Each run is a proof, so this belongs to the nightly's
  test-invariants-proof-backed job.

--- old
        uint64_t shift = s & ~nonzero_mask(top >> (64 - s));
--- new
        uint64_t shift = s & ~nonzero_mask(top >> (63 - s));
